432 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Found primarily in the canopies of trees or in deep forest areas\054 the Glidette are a race of squirrel\055like creatures with a unique membrane that trails from their wrists to their ankles\056 This skin\055like membrane allows the Glidette \050much like their Glider counterparts\051 to soar through the air\054 significantly slowing their fall and gliding to their destination safely\056\n\nIt is unknown what the relation is between Gliders and Glidette\056 While Glidette appear identical to Gliders\054 they tend to be slightly larger in size and have developed a level of intelligence that allows for communication and civilization to build\056 Otherwise\054 it is unknown whether the Glidette is simply a more advanced species of Glider or if they even share any relation at all\056 The Glidette view themselves as superior to Gliders in a sense that they feel obligated to protect their lesser\055developed counterparts\056 It is not uncommon to see colonies of Glidette provide shelter to the Gliders in the area\056\n\nGliding through the air with remarkable grace\054 Glidette often find themselves watching over their homelands from above\054 soaring from treetop to treetop in their travels\056 While most Glidette live their lives in small colonies in the jungles and forests\054 many still have come to build a different lifestyle among populated cities\056 These Glidette are quickly recruited by the cities to deliver mail and packages\054 as their ability to travel through the air is helpful to this cause\056 Highpeak City\047s postal system consists entirely of Glidette\054 specifically the Airpost family\056\n\nGlidette often only have one name\054 though Glidette families will often be referred to by titles reflective of their position\056 The Airpost Family in Highpeak City\054 for example\054 was named such by the local populace for their mail delivery expertise\056 It is not uncommon to find a Glidette with no family name\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 433 0 R
     /Pg 430 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

